  (text "SK6812 STATUS LEDs - 5V level shifter IC1, chain continues to header (TEENSY_LED_OUT / ESP32_LED_OUT)"
    (at 440 425 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 3 3)))
    (uuid "09e35d19-0edb-4dac-b7d6-d4e9c274be64"))

  (text "5V INPUT MUX - TPS2116: VIN1 = header 5V_IN (priority), VIN2 = Teensy VUSB (cut the VUSB-VIN pad on the Teensy). VOUT = 5V rail -> Teensy VIN, buck, LT3045"
    (at 1050 260 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 3 3)))
    (uuid "10f89715-10bb-4090-ab4e-fd07117f64bb"))

  (text "MCLK SOURCE - Y1 24.576 MHz (512 fs) feeds MCLK1 via R61; Teensy pin 23 reaches MCLK1 via R7. EXTERNAL-MCLK BUILD: populate R59 (Y1 on), DNP R60; firmware must set IOMUXC_GPR_GPR1 SAI1_MCLK_DIR=0 so pin 23 is an input. DEFAULT BUILD (no firmware yet): populate R60 (Y1 standby), DNP R59; Teensy drives MCLK1. Never both."
    (at 1005 1012 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 2 2)))
    (uuid "1651cdb1-1ccd-41e6-847b-e8753a76b9ee"))

  (text "TEENSY 4.1 - series terminations, SPI link to S3, CAN3, program lines"
    (at 90 195 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 3 3)))
    (uuid "1778f3fb-e106-4e3f-a633-9078aff30b6b"))

  (text "Header net naming: functions keep function names (TDM, SPDIF, USB, MIDI, DMX, LED, power); raw GPIO is named by MCU pin: T<n> = Teensy 4.1 pin n,\\nS3_IO<n> = ESP32-S3 GPIO n; an optional core function rides as a suffix (T14_SPDIF_OUT, T35_TX8, T18_SDA0, S3_IO43_TXD0, S3_IO47_SCL).\\nSimple backplane controls (no extra parts on the core): pot / volume knob = 10k linear between 3.3V (J1.9) and GND, wiper -> any Teensy analog pin\\n(T14=A0, T15=A1, T22=A8, T24=A10, T25=A11, T26=A12, T27=A13, T38=A14, T39=A15, T40=A16), 100 nF wiper-to-GND, analogRead() averaged.\\nS3-side pot: S3_IO2 / S3_IO8 / S3_IO9 / S3_IO10 only (ADC1; ADC2 pins are dead while WiFi is on). Switch / button: pin to GND, INPUT_PULLUP.\\nMore controls: 74HC4067 muxes on the analog pins, MCP23017 / TCA8418 on T17_SDA1 / T16_SCL1 (J2), SK6812 chain on J11."
    (at -120.65 648.97 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid "1dc7491f-54f6-4fbf-a601-b18a04cf9748"))

  (text "https://electronics.stackexchange.com/questions/310899/midi-out-thru-circuit-questions"
    (at 819.15 852.17 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (face "Arial")
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "2883ebde-686c-4a8f-8299-3cd4c467b2d4"))

  (text "J_ETH: Teensy 4.1 Ethernet pads 60-65 (R+ R- T+ T- LED GND, 2 mm 2x3 on the Teensy bottom).\\nPENDING: change U1 to project_sch:Teensy4.1 in eeschema, label pins 60=ETH_R+ 61=ETH_LED 62=ETH_T- 63=ETH_T+ 64=GND 65=ETH_R-,\\nand restore pads 60-65 in Teensy41_mod3 (they exist in Teensy41.kicad_mod). Magnetics + RJ45 live on the backplane."
    (at 560.07 300.99 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid "5944f1e9-0a8e-4425-8298-494c9cafeeb6"))

  (text "ESP32-S3 - WROOM-1-N16R2 (PCB antenna). IO4/6/7 = I2S master -> mux, IO16/IO35 = BT UART, IO46 = LED chain, IO19/20 = USB -> header, UART0 -> Teensy Serial7 + header"
    (at -310 583 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 3 3)))
    (uuid "5ea7a89c-d933-4b41-a047-3d87620b56cf"))

  (text "BLUETOOTH SINK - IDC777-1 (CONSIGNED part). I2S master into mux U21. UART to S3, RST/SYS_CTRL from SRC GPO1/GPO2, R72 = SYS_CTRL pulldown. Antenna end at a 100 mm board edge, copper-free keepout all layers."
    (at 1295 373 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 3 3)))
    (uuid "633dc3df-e7c4-4215-879c-c04579b5f89e"))

  (text "SRC4382 ASRC (CONSIGNED part) + 1.8V LDO. Port A <- mux (slave). Port B <-> Teensy I2S2 (4_BCLK2/3_LRCLK2/5_IN2/2_OUT2). GPO1..4 = BT_RST, BT_SYS_CTRL, BT_S3_SEL, AUX_SEL. ~RST = ESP32_EN. RX1-4 / TX pairs -> header J3."
    (at 1445 436 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 3 3)))
    (uuid "66264185-a624-4c16-aca4-93d97a470cc3"))

  (text "Low-Jitter Audio Clock"
    (at 1006.348 1013.968 0)
